  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "bugfix",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "Cohere2 previously left GatedMLP intermediate and output dtypes unspecified. The FP16 backend consequently defaulted its projection outputs to half precision; the change explicitly requests float32 for both.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_6106172d597c4b2b94e66486924d6b5c",
          "call_1d50e228752a4d7eaf259b95888191e1",
          "call_53037c84877c41e4b19051b759f648ab"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "The likely purpose is to reduce overflow in Cohere2 MLP projections and gated activations. Selecting float intermediates also selects an existing activation kernel that clamps its half-precision result, so this is more than a final output cast.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_6106172d597c4b2b94e66486924d6b5c",
          "call_fdbfa0c3ea9449d3a39021d96718f92f",
          "call_35e2747e928c448183ae9abe06de4f79"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "Every Cohere2 decoder layer receives the new settings. Checkpoint names, dimensions, weights, attention configuration and final vocabulary projection are unchanged.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_6106172d597c4b2b94e66486924d6b5c",
          "call_a7876656e783433391ebb44a980886cd"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The precision policy uses larger gate/up and down-output buffers, trading activation storage for numerical range. Neither its memory cost nor conversion or inference improvements were measured.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_1d50e228752a4d7eaf259b95888191e1",
          "call_53037c84877c41e4b19051b759f648ab"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "Read the Cohere2 introduction entry, which establishes the reused parallel decoder and shared calibration labels; the component-selection entry, which records Cohere2's text-component mapping; and the architecture-default chat entry, which concerns an unrelated method in the same file.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_6707cdc666af4af9b41477ffdd9b2926",
          "call_d14a593d5e7c425886b766d4a2f9af3e",
          "call_a2320414d50f45d8920e1f5fce3c4b14"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The padding-control entry records an inherited missing odd-element activation tail. Current source still processes pairs only, but Cohere2 retains the default 128-element projection padding, rather than exposing the entry's unpadded odd-size trigger.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_52a37d651a0f46f6a1b6a8c2cc0edcd2",
          "call_a7876656e783433391ebb44a980886cd",
          "call_1d50e228752a4d7eaf259b95888191e1",
          "call_fdbfa0c3ea9449d3a39021d96718f92f"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #34, \u201ctorch._C._LinAlgError on last layer of quant,\u201d reports Cohere2 conversion failure with infinite block.parallel.down inputs. Turboderp described possible post-activation overflow and suggested clamping. Issue #53, \u201cCommand A support,\u201d began as a support request and later reported similar conversion failures. Their relationship to this task is inferred from the matching architecture, projection path and numerical symptoms, not an explicit commit reference.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_35e2747e928c448183ae9abe06de4f79",
          "call_ddfa1ce99f744f65bbb99bf1db4daa46",
          "call_b9fe0afd13804115b1ab3d79345b0820",
          "call_6106172d597c4b2b94e66486924d6b5c"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #52, \u201cError converting moonshotai/Kimi-Dev-72B,\u201d contains turboderp's recommendation to request float GatedMLP output for a different architecture, followed by the reporter's successful-conversion report. This is an analogous precision remedy, not validation of this Cohere2 change. Issue #42, \u201cconverting to 3.0 bpw causes error; block state has 0 inf values and 34 NaN values,\u201d concerns Miqu and Command-R-Plus; its shared Linear path does not establish the same cause.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_9427004cee0e4395b842928dad7c726a",
          "call_d86797b1a2a1451cb773aa3bde0747ac",
          "call_197ee07fb49c4125956f00d4aff5c61a"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Other shared-file discussions were inspected: #7, \u201cquantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate,\u201d concerns extension loading; #55, \u201cPossible GLM4 32B regression,\u201d concerns fused-weight construction; and #48, \u201c`RuntimeError` when requesting logprobs with Gemma 3 models,\u201d concerns logits dimensions. Their inferred overlap is through imported modules or shared utility files, not evidence that this precision change remedies them.",
