    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Cohere2 MLP precision boundaries",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Cohere2Model.__init__ adds interm_dtype=torch.float and out_dtype=torch.float to each GatedMLP. GatedMLP stores these independently: intermediate dtype configures gate/up Linear outputs, while output dtype configures each down projection and the returned result.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_6106172d597c4b2b94e66486924d6b5c",
              "call_1d50e228752a4d7eaf259b95888191e1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "This does not make the entire MLP float32. ParallelDecoderBlock normalizes its shared branch input to half. Gate/up now produce float outputs, but GatedMLP allocates a separate half activation buffer and computes silu(gate) * up into it. That half buffer feeds down; down outputs and any slice accumulation use the requested float dtype.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_864415ae86904791b8139ad23834f7ab",
              "call_1d50e228752a4d7eaf259b95888191e1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The two settings protect different boundaries. interm_dtype selects silu_mul's float-input branch, which evaluates activation and multiplication in float, converts to half, then clamps to \u00b165504. The half-input branch instead uses half2 arithmetic without that clamp. out_dtype separately avoids forcing the down-projection result back into half before residual addition.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_fdbfa0c3ea9449d3a39021d96718f92f",
              "call_1d50e228752a4d7eaf259b95888191e1",
              "call_864415ae86904791b8139ad23834f7ab"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For unquantized LinearFP16, output dtype resolves as call override, stored dtype, then half. With half input and float output, forward selects ext.hgemm rather than its same-dtype torch.matmul branch. hgemm requires half operands and uses cublasGemmEx with float output and CUBLAS_COMPUTE_32F. Thus the change requests wider projection results without changing stored weights to float32.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_53037c84877c41e4b19051b759f648ab",
              "call_20a9d123342e44e88f66a928c1502466",
              "call_197ee07fb49c4125956f00d4aff5c61a"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Linear also forwards its stored output dtype into loaded or newly converted LinearEXL3 instances. LinearEXL3 allocates that dtype in both reconstructed-matmul and direct-quantized routes. Its existing reconstruction selection remains unchanged; this commit changes output precision, not that dispatch rule.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_197ee07fb49c4125956f00d4aff5c61a",
              "call_f5a1acf168ed414893816edb25b77158",
              "call_6106172d597c4b2b94e66486924d6b5c"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The direct consumer, ParallelDecoderBlock.forward, adds the MLP result in place to the existing residual; the new float MLP output does not itself replace the residual with a float tensor. Its prefill shortcut still returns before executing the MLP. The explicit forward dtype override remains supported by to2 and takes priority over the configured return dtype.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_864415ae86904791b8139ad23834f7ab",
              "call_1d50e228752a4d7eaf259b95888191e1",
              "call_8b62cf78df534ad1bb2abb548006a001"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library scalar check decoded 65504 as the largest finite binary16 value. A modeled gated product of 80000 converted to infinity in half but saturated to 65504 with the float-path clamp. A second example, gate=70000 and up=0, produced NaN after first overflowing the gate to half, versus zero when retaining the gate in wider arithmetic. These illustrate distinct projection and activation hazards; Python arithmetic does not reproduce CUDA's float32 approximations.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_bb877c96f5a144ce99758855a1aea159"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "All three inspected configurations select Cohere2ForCausalLM and silu, so the unconditional settings apply model by model: CohereLabs/c4ai-command-a-03-2025 uses hidden/intermediate widths 12288/36864 and 64 layers; c4ai-command-r7b-12-2024 uses 4096/14336 and 32 layers; c4ai-command-r7b-arabic-02-2025 likewise uses 4096/14336 and 32 layers. Their declared bfloat16 checkpoint dtype does not override these constructor arguments.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_21e868c7a20a4b108598705d3c6eb99b",
              "call_b6e4c07738014ab8bfb7ca19e4de3b08",
              "call_98b97dc226b34086adaba0d52b897abe",
              "call_a7876656e783433391ebb44a980886cd",
              "call_6106172d597c4b2b94e66486924d6b5c"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Representative layer-zero headers contain the unchanged model.layers.0.mlp gate_proj/up_proj weights with shapes [36864,12288] for Command A and [14336,4096] for each R7B; down_proj has the reversed dimensions. These agree with the existing output-row/input-column loading layout. The inspected MLP groups contain no biases or weight_scale_inv tensors, which Linear requests optionally; primary weights exist, so fused fallback is unnecessary. No unused stored tensor was identified in these inspected header subsets.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9f948b2a043840efb098e22de643954a",
              "call_4626d262dabf4538bb0f7207332c6a82",
              "call_810ae143b6f44707a07468e8958317a1",
              "call_197ee07fb49c4125956f00d4aff5c61a",
              "call_a7876656e783433391ebb44a980886cd"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [],
    "summary": "Requests float32 gate/up projection results and MLP outputs throughout Cohere2, selecting an existing float activation-and-clamp path while retaining half activation inputs to down projections. Numerical benefits remain unmeasured."
  },
